HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4ce7f693, "` is only called by name, its `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_465aa6cc, "` marked `@` at the call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_69659380, "\302\2474.8: the `@` is written at the call too, so a call that changes an argument never looks like one that reads it, and a value called `f(x)` would hide it. To hand the work around as a value, write a function without `@` that returns the new value \342\200\224 `function next(n: i64) -> i64` \342\200\224 and assign what it returns");
