HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_46fb19cd, "a function value does not change this argument \342\200\224 the `@` says it does");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_45dd8224, "no function type carries an `@` (\302\247 9), so a value is always called with plain arguments; a function that changes its argument is called by name, `f(@x)`");
