HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2158d1d3, "hands back a handle of type `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7db17313, "` inside `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4c23e1f7, "unmarked_handle_producer");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3b51e2b3, " and does not say whether the program owes it \342\200\224 `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7acff04b, "` takes one back");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_784c5861, ", so this binding has said how the `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_776aaacd, "` ends and not how it begins");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4c917f25, "write `acquires ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_51cfbb32, "` if the call gives the handle away and the program must return it, or `borrows` if the library keeps it and the program owes nothing. No C header states which, so the binding author states it: `sqlite3_prepare_v2` gives a statement and `sqlite3_next_stmt` lends one, and their C signatures are the same shape");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_e815a81, "one mark answers for the whole value, however many handles it carries: C frees a composite with one call, and `");
