HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4b90fae9, "`; bind that function instead, and its prototype holds the `const`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_34fbaf35, "` is declared `cstr lent`, and ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6771426f, " \342\200\224 C reads what a call hands it there as whatever type it asks for, and does not promise to leave it alone");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_737856d6, "\302\2474.20: `s.cstr()` lends the string's own bytes, and they may be shared with other values \342\200\224 a C write through them changes values this program never passed to C, and on a literal it aborts");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7289a69c, "hand C a copy it may write instead: declare `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2dfd6c26, ": cstr` without `lent`, pass it a lease, `x: cstr @= text.lease()`, and end the lease with `end_lease(@x)` once the call returns");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1f102a62, "` is an `@` parameter, and ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6441fc03, " \342\200\224 C reads the pointer there as whatever type it asks for and writes as much as that type holds, so nothing holds it to the width this program lends");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_59025b69, "\302\2474.19: what an `@` parameter points at is held to the header's own type, its width and sign, and past a header's `...` the header gives none: a wider write overwrites what lies beside a field or an element, and a narrower one leaves part of the cell as it was");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_20bdb2f5, "` at the C type `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2ab80d28, "` writes through it and handing it on to `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3ed9a73b, "`; bind that function instead, and its prototype holds the width");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7e7905e3, "` is declared `counted_by`, and ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2177e6fe, " \342\200\224 C counts in what its pointer points at, and there the pointer has no type, so no count can be held to what is lent");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_26d6eee8, "\302\2474.19: a counted lend hands C the program's own bytes, a field, an array or a record, and C counts them in what its pointer points at; past a header's `...` none of them can be held to a count, so declare `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_37e347d1, ": ptr` and hand it memory C gave you");
