HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3d501578, " *` points at a different width or sign \342\200\224 clang read the header, and C writes back exactly the bytes the header expects");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_f65f7aa, "\302\2474.19: a C out-parameter is an `@` parameter, and what it points at is held to the header's own width and sign \342\200\224 `u64` where it says `size_t *`, `i32` where it says `int *`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_419319f1, "` has no name in this language yet \342\200\224 declare the parameter at its width and sign, and say which in a comment beside the declaration");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_69aad865, "` as `@");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_72d9c3c7, "not a void-pointee assertion");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_554dd4c9, "which has no width \342\200\224 nothing can be written back into a cell the header describes as sizeless");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_34c2f713, "not a depth assertion");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3da9055f, "with `@`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_48d7afc8, ", so C is handed the address of the program's cell, and the header's `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_444a8660, " *` points at `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_73831c04, "` \342\200\224 one pointer, which C reads as the handle itself, never as a cell to write one into");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_747419ab, "\302\2474.19: `@` on a handle or a `ptr` is for a parameter the header spells `T **`, one that writes a pointer back into the cell; a parameter spelled `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_51ce0507, " *` takes the handle, so pass it without `@`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4fbb98ab, "if the header does write a pointer back, it is the header that is short by one `*`, and the binding is right \342\200\224 say so beside the declaration and change the header, never the mark");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6ef07ac1, "` without `@`: `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5c46481d, "incomplete type '");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_21766f6c, "which the header leaves incomplete \342\200\224 C keeps it opaque on purpose, and only C can size it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_40db2436, "at a width");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_10a01a6c, "\302\2474.19: a pointer to something the header does not size is bound as `ptr` \342\200\224 declare `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7f8ac681, ": ptr`, hold the address C hands you (or the address of a `record` you declared with the layout the library documents), and pass it");
